    ('229b6db0336c', "\n\n**Vulnerability reporting threshold (no junk, but do not miss real findings)**\n\nREPORT (with evidence; do not drop it just because you did not get a shell):\n- XSS: reflected / stored / DOM all count. Report whenever you have evidence of real rendering and execution (browser screenshot, console output, DOM change), including self-contained payloads; state the trigger path and preconditions (interaction required, HttpOnly / CSP).\n- Blind SSRF: report with out-of-band callback evidence (DNS/HTTP to your own listener or Collaborator), or when you can prove reachability of the internal network / cloud metadata / an unintended host, even without an echo; state the exfiltration channel and follow-on options.\n- Blind injection without echo: report whenever there is reproducible time / boolean / out-of-band side-channel evidence; seeing data is not required.\n- Chained exploits: a weak link that is genuinely part of a chain may be reported, but summary/evidence must state how A's output makes B possible, the real evidence for every step, the final impact and the severity rationale; a chain that did not actually complete is not a chain.\n\nDO NOT REPORT (and do not pile them up as 'pending findings'):\n- Version / fingerprint disclosure, missing HTTP security headers, directory listings or static leaks such as robots.txt, purely informational notices.\n- **Unauthorised access with no real impact**: anonymous access that returns only public information, health checks, empty lists, dictionary/enumeration listings, or only your own test data; no sensitive data readable and no business write or privilege-crossing effect.\n- **Unauthorised low-value information disclosure**: internal field/table names, component versions, stack traces, public configuration -- where no credentials/keys and no user or business data are obtained and nothing can serve as a prerequisite for further exploitation.\n- Self-XSS you can only paste to yourself, with no user interaction path.\n- A parameter that looks like a URL but has no callback or side-channel evidence ('suspected SSRF'); blind-injection guesses with neither echo nor side channel.\n- Issues inferred only from CVE / patch comparison, and 'issues' that only matter after obtaining credentials of the same privilege level.\n\nUnauthorised-access judgement: sensitive data (user / business / credentials or keys) obtained, or a write / privilege-crossing operation is possible -> report; merely being able to open it with valueless content -> do not report; usable as a chain prerequisite (internal path, internal service address, working credentials) -> report as a chained exploit and write the whole chain in evidence.\nIf unsure, note it as suspect in TodoWrite and do not emit a finding; keep only high / critical severities, and rate chains by final impact."),  # 009 agent/finding_workflow.go L26 | **漏洞上报门槛（别刷垃圾，也别漏真洞）**  该报的（有证据就报，别因为没直接拿到权限就丢
    ('efd65e024cf0', '\n\n**Reporting threshold (strict red-team variant: RCE and three-element data leaks only)**\n- Report only two classes: (1) RCE (command/code execution, deserialisation, upload-to-shell, template injection executing code, with real command output or callback proof); (2) information disclosure of the THREE ELEMENTS (national ID / mobile number / bank card number, including name, address, account+password combinations that allow impersonation or login; you must actually retrieve the data and show masked samples).\n- Other vulnerabilities (XSS / SSRF / injection without data / unauthorised access returning empty data / low-value information disclosure) are recorded only as intermediate chain steps in facts and the summary -- **do not call report_finding**; only when they finally lead to RCE or a three-element leak do you report the final result together with the chain.\n- If unsure, note it as suspect in TodoWrite and do not emit a finding; severity: RCE and three-element leaks are high/critical, chains are rated by final impact.'),  # 010 agent/finding_workflow.go L31 | **上报门槛（攻防 agent 严格版：只报 RCE 与三要素泄露）** - 只报两类：① 
